==Cast and characters==
{{Main|List of Arrow characters|List of supporting Arrow characters|List of Arrowverse cast members}}

* [[Stephen Amell]] as [[Oliver Queen (Arrowverse)|Oliver Queen / Arrow / Green Arrow]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=August 19, 2019 |title='Arrow' Star Stephen Amell To Headline Starz Wrestling Drama Series 'Heels' |url=https://deadline.com/2019/08/stephen-amell-star-heels-wrestling-drama-starz-picked-up-series-order-mike-omalley-1202670994/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190820001018/https://deadline.com/2019/08/stephen-amell-star-heels-wrestling-drama-starz-picked-up-series-order-mike-omalley-1202670994/ |archive-date=August 20, 2019 |access-date=August 26, 2019 |website=Deadline Hollywood}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Arrow: Stephen Amell Teases Heartbreaking Dialogue From Final Season Premiere |url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/08/25/arrow-stephen-amell-season-8-premiere-dialogue/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190826024403/https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/08/25/arrow-stephen-amell-season-8-premiere-dialogue/ |archive-date=August 26, 2019 |access-date=August 26, 2019 |website=ComicBook}}</ref> a billionaire playboy turned hooded vigilante-hero who is initially known as the "Hood", "Vigilante", and simply "Arrow". He is based on the DC Comics character [[Green Arrow]]. He survives on an isolated island for five years after the sinking of his father's yacht. Oliver returns to his home city with a mission—to right the wrongs of his father and save the city from the crime that has grown in his absence. Amell was one of the first actors to audition for the role, and Kreisberg felt that he "hit the target from the outset" and "everyone else just paled in comparison".<ref name="Canada"/> In season six's finale, Oliver confesses he's the Green Arrow and is sent to prison where he's known as "Inmate 4587". The actor, who was already in shape from ''[[Rent-a-Goalie]]'', did physical fitness training at Tempest Freerunning Academy in Reseda, California. Amell received archery training as well, which included watching a video on how archery has been displayed inaccurately or poorly in television and film before learning the basics of shooting a bow.<ref name="Canada"/><ref>{{cite web |title=Stephen Amell brings Arrow to small screen |url=http://o.canada.com/entertainment/television/stephen-amell-brings-arrow-to-small-screen |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131024053733/http://o.canada.com/entertainment/television/stephen-amell-brings-arrow-to-small-screen/ |archive-date=October 24, 2013 |access-date=April 3, 2016 |website=canada.com}}</ref> For Amell, the appeal of portraying Queen was that he saw multiple roles tied to the same character: "There's Queen the casual playboy; Queen the wounded hero; Queen the brooding Hamlet; Queen the lover; Queen the man of action, and so on".<ref name="Canada"/> Amell also portrays [[Dark Arrow]] (Oliver's Earth-X doppelganger) in the sixth season's crossover "[[Crisis on Earth-X]]".<ref>{{Cite news |date=October 17, 2017 |title=Green Arrow Faces Prometheus-X in Arrowverse Crossover Photo |url=https://www.cbr.com/green-arrow-prometheus-x-arrowverse-crossover/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180521104349/https://www.cbr.com/green-arrow-prometheus-x-arrowverse-crossover/ |archive-date=May 21, 2018 |access-date=May 20, 2018 |work=CBR}}</ref>
* [[Katie Cassidy]] as [[Laurel Lance (Arrowverse Earth-1)|Laurel Lance / Black Canary]] (seasons 1–4; guest: season 5–8) and [[Laurel Lance (Arrowverse Earth-2)|Laurel Lance / Black Siren / Black Canary]] (seasons 6–8;{{efn|Although Cassidy is billed as a "special appearance" in [[Arrow season 8|season 8]], she is still considered a series regular for the season.<ref>{{cite web |last=Mitovich |first=Matt Webb |date=October 16, 2019 |title=Arrow/The Flash: Burning Qs Answered About Earth-Two, the New Hood, Canaries Spinoff Set-Up and More |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/the-flash-earth-two-destroyed-arrow-season-8-premiere-1114186/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191016201807/https://tvline.com/2019/10/16/the-flash-earth-two-destroyed-arrow-season-8-premiere/ |archive-date=October 16, 2019 |access-date=October 17, 2019 |work=[[TVLine]]}}</ref>}} recurring: season 5),<ref>{{Cite web |date=August 19, 2019 |title=Arrow's Katie Cassidy Rodgers Pitched a Birds of Prey Spinoff to The CW |url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/08/19/arrow-spoilers-final-season-spinoff-birds-of-prey-katie-cassidy/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190826192840/https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/08/19/arrow-spoilers-final-season-spinoff-birds-of-prey-katie-cassidy/ |archive-date=August 26, 2019 |access-date=August 26, 2019 |website=DC}}</ref> based on the DC Comics character of the same name,<ref>{{cite web |last=Jeffrey |first=Morgan |date=March 11, 2013 |title=''Arrow'' exec on Black Canary debut: 'It has to be earned' |url=http://www.digitalspy.com/tv/s206/arrow/news/a464829/arrow-exec-on-black-canary-debut-it-has-to-be-earned.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130509125206/http://www.digitalspy.com/tv/s206/arrow/news/a464829/arrow-exec-on-black-canary-debut-it-has-to-be-earned.html |archive-date=May 9, 2013 |access-date=April 16, 2013 |work=Digital Spy}}</ref><ref name="CassidyCast">{{cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=February 15, 2012 |title=Katie Cassidy Set As Female Lead In CW Pilot ''Arrow'' |url=https://deadline.com/2012/02/katie-cassidy-set-as-female-lead-in-cw-pilot-arrow-231444/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130923100458/http://www.deadline.com/2012/02/katie-cassidy-set-as-female-lead-in-cw-pilot-arrow/ |archive-date=September 23, 2013 |access-date=April 16, 2013 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> an attorney turned vigilante and former girlfriend of Oliver Queen. Cassidy said she was drawn to the show by Berlanti, Nutter, Kreisberg, and Guggenheim, whom she called smart, creative, and edgy. She was the first primary character to be cast.<ref name="KCint2">{{cite web |last=Byrne |first=Craig |date=August 7, 2012 |title=GreenArrowTV Interview With Katie Cassidy, "Laurel Lance" |url=http://www.greenarrowtv.com/greenarrowtv-interview-with-katie-cassidy-laurel-lance/11422 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131202222120/http://www.greenarrowtv.com/greenarrowtv-interview-with-katie-cassidy-laurel-lance/11422 |archive-date=December 2, 2013 |access-date=November 27, 2013 |work=GreenArrowTV.com}}</ref> Cassidy sees her character as a "caregiver" to her family, which led her to become an attorney. She said, "I think that she's very, very driven, and she has a huge heart ... she's sensitive. She has really strong morals and values, and she expects everybody to live up to them the way that she does".<ref name="KCint">{{cite web |last=Byrne |first=Craig |date=July 23, 2012 |title=Arrow's Canary: Interview With Katie Cassidy, "Laurel Lance" |url=http://www.greenarrowtv.com/arrows-canary-interview-with-katie-cassidy-laurel-lance/11348 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131202230458/http://www.greenarrowtv.com/arrows-canary-interview-with-katie-cassidy-laurel-lance/11348 |archive-date=December 2, 2013 |access-date=November 27, 2013 |work=GreenArrowTV.com}}</ref> The Earth-1 version of the character dies near the end of season four, but Cassidy returned as a series regular from season six onward as the Earth-2 version of the character who first appeared in the spin-off show ''[[The Flash (2014 TV series)|The Flash]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mitovich |first=Matt Webb |date=March 27, 2017 |title=Arrow: Katie Cassidy to Return as Series Regular for Season 6, Playing [Spoiler] |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/arrow-season-6-katie-cassidy-series-regular-black-siren-811654/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170328013523/http://tvline.com/2017/03/27/arrow-season-6-katie-cassidy-series-regular-black-siren/ |archive-date=March 28, 2017 |access-date=March 28, 2017 |website=TVLine}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Wagmeister |first=Elizabeth |date=March 27, 2017 |title=Katie Cassidy Returning to 'Arrow' for Good as Black Siren |url=https://variety.com/2017/tv/news/katie-cassidy-returning-arrow-black-siren-season-6-the-cw-1202017139/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170328195400/http://variety.com/2017/tv/news/katie-cassidy-returning-arrow-black-siren-season-6-the-cw-1202017139/ |archive-date=March 28, 2017 |access-date=March 28, 2017 |work=Variety}}</ref>
* [[Colin Donnell]] as [[Tommy Merlyn (Arrowverse)|Tommy Merlyn]] (season 1; recurring: seasons 7–8; guest: seasons 2–3 and 6), Oliver's best friend,<ref name="DonnellCast">{{cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=February 21, 2012 |title=Titus Welliver To Star In NBC's ''Midnight Sun'', CW's ''Arrow'' Adds Colin Donnell |url=https://deadline.com/2012/02/titus-welliver-to-star-in-nbcs-midnight-sun-cws-arrow-adds-colin-donnell-234108/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131114210058/http://www.deadline.com/2012/02/titus-welliver-to-star-in-nbcs-midnight-sun-cws-arrow-adds-colin-donnell/ |archive-date=November 14, 2013 |access-date=November 19, 2013 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> the son of [[Malcolm Merlyn (Arrowverse)|Malcolm Merlyn]] and boyfriend to Laurel Lance. His character dies in season one's finale but Donnell reprises his role as hallucinations and flashbacks in subsequent seasons and also portrays his Earth-X doppelganger Prometheus and a posthumous impersonation by [[Human Target]] in season six. Donnell returns in the eighth and final season as Merlyn's Earth-2 doppelgänger and is brought back to life by Oliver when he restored the multiverse in the "[[Crisis on Infinite Earths (Arrowverse)|Crisis on Infinite Earths]]" crossover event.
* [[David Ramsey]] as [[John Diggle (Arrowverse)|John Diggle / Spartan]],<ref>{{cite web |date=November 12, 2015 |title=Marc Guggenheim Confirms Diggle's Codename is Spartan&nbsp;– DC Comics Movies&nbsp;— DCComicsMovie.com |url=http://dccomicsmovie.com/marc-guggenheim-confirms-diggles-codename-is-spartan/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160308002112/http://dccomicsmovie.com/marc-guggenheim-confirms-diggles-codename-is-spartan/ |archive-date=March 8, 2016 |access-date=January 28, 2016}}</ref> Oliver's partner, confidant, and bodyguard, who becomes part of their vigilante team.<ref name="RamseyCast">{{cite news |last=Levine |first=Stuart |date=February 8, 2012 |title=Ramsey cast in CW's ''Arrow'' pilot |url=https://variety.com/2012/tv/news/ramsey-cast-in-cw-s-arrow-pilot-1118049941/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140717191653/http://variety.com/2012/tv/news/ramsey-cast-in-cw-s-arrow-pilot-1118049941/ |archive-date=July 17, 2014 |access-date=November 19, 2013 |work=Variety}}</ref> Named after comic book writer Andy Diggle, and created specifically for the show, Diggle was designed to be Oliver's "equal in many respects". Guggenheim further explained that Diggle's mutual abilities are a means of setting him up early in the series as a confidant for Oliver's vigilante persona.<ref>{{cite web |last=Byrne |first=Craig |date=July 19, 2012 |title=Interview: Marc Guggenheim Unlocks The Secrets & Connections In Arrow |url=http://www.greenarrowtv.com/interview-marc-guggenheim-unlocks-the-secrets-connections-in-arrow/11329 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131203002406/http://www.greenarrowtv.com/interview-marc-guggenheim-unlocks-the-secrets-connections-in-arrow/11329 |archive-date=December 3, 2013 |access-date=November 27, 2013 |work=GreenArrowTV.com}}</ref>
* [[Willa Holland]] as [[Thea Queen|Thea Queen / Speedy]] (seasons 1–6; recurring: season 8; guest: season 7), Oliver's younger half-sister; based on a DC Comics character with similar traits.<ref name="HollandCast">{{cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=February 15, 2012 |title=''Arrow'' & Nick Stoller Comedy Add To Casts |url=https://deadline.com/2012/02/arrow-nick-stoller-comedy-add-to-casts-231747/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131202222053/http://www.deadline.com/2012/02/arrow-nick-stoller-comedy-add-to-casts/ |archive-date=December 2, 2013 |access-date=November 19, 2013 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> The character is later revealed to be the daughter of Malcolm Merlyn. Holland exited the series in season six. Guggenheim stated that the door is always open for Holland to reprise her role as Thea.<ref>{{Cite news |title='Arrow' boss on that shocking cast departure |url=https://ew.com/tv/2018/03/29/arrow-willa-holland-thea-exit/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180330233751/http://ew.com/tv/2018/03/29/arrow-willa-holland-thea-exit/ |archive-date=March 30, 2018 |access-date=April 3, 2018 |work=EW.com}}</ref> After departing the series in the sixth season, Holland returned in a special guest star role during season seven.<ref name="tvguide.com">{{Cite web |date=February 4, 2019 |title=Arrow's 150th Episode: Holy Cameos, Batman! {{!}} TV Guide |url=https://www.tvguide.com/news/arrow-150th-episode-thea-lance-roy-sara-sin-rory-return/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190205201858/https://www.tvguide.com/news/arrow-150th-episode-thea-lance-roy-sara-sin-rory-return/ |archive-date=February 5, 2019 |access-date=February 7, 2019 |website=TVGuide.com}}</ref> [[Melissa Benoist]] had auditioned to portray Thea but was ultimately cast as Supergirl instead.{{Citation needed|date=March 2026}}
* [[Susanna Thompson]] as [[Moira Queen (Arrowverse)|Moira Queen]] (seasons 1–2; guest: seasons 5 & 8), Oliver and Thea's mother.<ref name="ThompsonCast">{{cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=February 14, 2012 |title=PILOT CASTINGS: Susanna Thompson Joins ''Arrow'', ''Nashville'' & ''County'' Add Actors |url=https://deadline.com/2012/02/pilot-castings-susanna-thompson-joins-arrow-nashville-county-add-actors-230983/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131105151451/http://www.deadline.com/2012/02/pilot-castings-susanna-thompson-joins-arrow-nashville-county-add-actors/ |archive-date=November 5, 2013 |access-date=November 19, 2013 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> She is murdered at the end of season two,<ref>{{Cite news |date=September 29, 2016 |title=Arrow: Moira Queen Returning For 100th Episode |url=https://screenrant.com/arrow-moira-queen-return-susanna-thompson/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180504225339/https://screenrant.com/arrow-moira-queen-return-susanna-thompson/ |archive-date=May 4, 2018 |access-date=May 3, 2018 |work=Screen Rant}}</ref> but was brought back by Oliver after he restored the multiverse.
* [[Paul Blackthorne]] as [[Quentin Lance]] (seasons 1–6; recurring: season 8; guest: season 7), Laurel and [[Sara Lance]]'s father and Starling City police detective.<ref name="Blackthorne/SheridanCast">{{cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=March 2, 2012 |title=''The River''{{'s}} Paul Blackthorne Joins ''Arrow'', Jamey Sheridan Set To Play Arrow's Dad |url=https://deadline.com/2012/03/paul-blackthorne-arrow-cast-jamey-sheridan-arrows-dad-238838/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131103072103/http://www.deadline.com/2012/03/paul-blackthorne-arrow-cast-jamey-sheridan-arrows-dad/ |archive-date=November 3, 2013 |access-date=October 28, 2013 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> The character is partly based on the DC Comics character [[Larry Lance]]. The character dies in the sixth-season finale,<ref>{{Cite news |title='Arrow' Star Paul Blackthorne to Exit After Season 6 |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/arrow-star-paul-blackthorne-exit-season-6-1107665 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180502231355/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/arrow-star-paul-blackthorne-exit-season-6-1107665 |archive-date=May 2, 2018 |access-date=May 2, 2018 |work=The Hollywood Reporter}}</ref><ref name="tvguide.com"/> but his death is averted after Oliver restored the multiverse.
* [[Emily Bett Rickards]] as [[Felicity Smoak (Arrowverse)|Felicity Smoak / Overwatch]] (seasons 2–7; recurring: season 1; guest: season 8),<ref name=FelicityOracleCodenameReveal>{{cite magazine |title=Arrow reveals Felicity's codename |url=https://www.ew.com/article/2016/01/27/arrow-felicity-codename-overwatch-oracle |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160130230027/http://www.ew.com/article/2016/01/27/arrow-felicity-codename-overwatch-oracle |archive-date=January 30, 2016 |access-date=January 28, 2016 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref><ref name="RickardsCast">{{cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=August 10, 2012 |title=Shiri Appleby Poised To Recur On NBC's ''Chicago Fire'' & More TV Castings |url=https://deadline.com/2012/08/shiri-appleby-poised-to-recur-on-nbcs-chicago-fire-more-tv-castings-316918/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140301085431/http://www.deadline.com/2012/08/shiri-appleby-poised-to-recur-on-nbcs-chicago-fire-more-tv-castings/ |archive-date=March 1, 2014 |access-date=February 14, 2013 |website=Deadline Hollywood}}</ref> an IT technician at Queen Consolidated who later becomes part of Oliver's vigilante team, adopting the codename 'Overwatch'.<ref name=FelicityOracleCodenameReveal/> She is loosely based on the character [[Felicity Smoak|of the same name]] from the comic series ''[[Firestorm (character)|Firestorm]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wilson |first=Matt D. |date=July 1, 2013 |title=Gerry Conway Starts Blog Aimed at Fair Compensation For DC Character Creators |url=http://comicsalliance.com/tags/felicity-smoak/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150906085511/http://comicsalliance.com/gerry-conway-blog-dc-comics-character-fair-compensation-fans/ |archive-date=September 6, 2015 |website=[[ComicsAlliance]] |publisher=[[Townsquare Media]] |quote=Gerry Conway, the writer who co-created the character with artist Rafael Kayanan in a 1984 issue of ''Firestorm''.}}</ref> The character goes on to develop a romantic relationship with Oliver, with the pair marrying during the "[[Crisis on Earth-X]]" crossover event. She becomes stepmother to Oliver's son, [[William Clayton (Arrowverse)|William]], and mother to their daughter [[Mia Smoak|Mia]]. During season four she worked as CEO of Palmer Tech, and in season seven founded her own company, Smoak Technologies. Rickards was initially cast as a one-off guest star but was promoted to a series regular for season two, after becoming a recurring character throughout season one.<ref>{{cite web |last=Marnell |first=Blair |date=February 12, 2013 |title=Emily Bett Rickards Promoted For 'Arrow' Season 2 |url=http://www.craveonline.com/tv/articles/204841-emily-bett-rickards-promoted-for-arrow-season-2 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150701122328/http://www.craveonline.com/tv/articles/204841-emily-bett-rickards-promoted-for-arrow-season-2 |archive-date=July 1, 2015 |access-date=February 22, 2013 |work=[[CraveOnline]]}}</ref> Describing the character's personality, Rickards stated "Felicity is really focused, and I think that focus can be overpowering. The whole bubbly/awkward thing is a product of the focus. I don't think they're parts on their own."<ref>{{cite web |last=Phegley |first=Kiel |date=October 30, 2013 |title=Emily Bett Rickards Brings Personality To "Arrow's" Felicity Smoak |url=https://www.cbr.com/emily-bett-rickards-brings-personality-to-arrows-felicity-smoak/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170421004401/https://www.cbr.com/emily-bett-rickards-brings-personality-to-arrows-felicity-smoak/ |archive-date=April 21, 2017 |access-date=October 12, 2018 |work=Comic Book Review}}</ref> In March 2019, Rickards announced she would be leaving the series ahead of its final season.<ref>{{cite web |last=Bennett |first=Anita |date=March 30, 2019 |title='Arrow' Actress Emily Bett Rickards Announces Exit Ahead Of Final Season |url=https://deadline.com/2019/03/arrow-actress-emily-bett-rickards-announces-exit-ahead-of-final-season-1202585660/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190330210601/https://deadline.com/2019/03/arrow-actress-emily-bett-rickards-announces-exit-ahead-of-final-season-1202585660/ |archive-date=March 30, 2019 |access-date=March 30, 2019 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> She returned as a special guest star for the series finale.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mittovich |first=Matt Webb |date=November 1, 2019 |title=''Arrow''{{'s}} Series Finale: Emily Bett Rickards Returns for Series Finale – Will Olicity Reunite? |url=https://tvline.com/2019/11/01/arrow-emily-bett-rickards-returns-series-finale-felicity/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191101171650/https://tvline.com/2019/11/01/arrow-emily-bett-rickards-returns-series-finale-felicity/ |archive-date=November 1, 2019 |access-date=November 1, 2019 |website=[[TVLine]]}}</ref>
* [[Colton Haynes]] as [[Roy Harper (Arrowverse)|Roy Harper / Arsenal]] (seasons 2–3 and 7; recurring: seasons 1 & 8; guest: seasons 4 & 6), a character based on the DC Comics character of the same name.<ref name="HaynesCast">{{cite web |last=Holbrook |first=Damian |date=December 11, 2012 |title=Exclusive: ''Teen Wolf'' Vet Colton Haynes Joins ''Arrow'' as ... Who?! |url=https://www.tvguide.com/News/Arrow-Colton-Haynes-1057668.aspx |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141006205311/http://www.tvguide.com/news/arrow-colton-haynes-1057668.aspx |archive-date=October 6, 2014 |access-date=December 12, 2012 |work=TV Guide}}</ref> He is also Thea Queen's romantic partner. Haynes was moved to series regular status at the beginning of season two, following his recurring appearance in season one.<ref>{{cite news |last=Goldberg |first=Lesley |date=March 13, 2013 |title=''Arrow'' Promotes Colton Haynes to Series Regular for Season 2 |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/arrow-colton-haynes-series-regular-season-2-428346 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130316011439/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/arrow-colton-haynes-series-regular-season-2-428346 |archive-date=March 16, 2013 |access-date=March 13, 2013 |work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> Haynes left the series after season three when his contract ended, and later appears as a guest star in the fourth, sixth, and eighth seasons<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Abrams |first1=Natalie |date=April 15, 2015 |title=Arrow twist: Scoop on the big exit |url=https://www.ew.com/article/2015/04/15/arrow-twist-scoop-big-exit |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150416052646/http://www.ew.com/article/2015/04/15/arrow-twist-scoop-big-exit |archive-date=April 16, 2015 |access-date=April 15, 2015 |magazine=Entertainment Weekly}}</ref> (attributing his departure from to his mental and physical health at that time),<ref>{{cite magazine |date=May 5, 2016 |title=Colton Haynes gets honest about life after Arrow |url=https://www.ew.com/article/2016/05/05/colton-haynes-interview |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160812024938/http://www.ew.com/article/2016/05/05/colton-haynes-interview |archive-date=August 12, 2016 |access-date=August 2, 2016 |magazine=Entertainment Weekly}}</ref> but returned as a regular for season seven.<ref>{{cite web |date=April 9, 2018 |title='Arrow': Colton Haynes Officially Returning as Season 7 Regular |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/arrow-colton-haynes-returning-as-season-7-regular-1100766 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180409212652/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/arrow-colton-haynes-returning-as-season-7-regular-1100766 |archive-date=April 9, 2018 |access-date=April 9, 2018 |work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref>
* [[Manu Bennett]] as [[Slade Wilson (Arrowverse)|Slade Wilson / Deathstroke]] (season 2; recurring: season 1; guest: seasons 3 & 5–6), Oliver's former mentor on Lian Yu who becomes a masked mercenary. He is based on the DC Comics character of the same name.<ref name="BennettCast">{{cite magazine |last=Hibberd |first=James |date=November 30, 2012 |title=''Arrow'' casts ''Spartacus'' actor |url=https://ew.com/article/2012/11/30/arrow-manu-bennett/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210518172517/https://ew.com/article/2012/11/30/arrow-manu-bennett/ |archive-date=May 18, 2021 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> Bennett was initially cast as a recurring character for season one,<ref name="BennettCast" /> before receiving series regular status during season two.<ref>{{cite news |last=Goldberg |first=Lesley |date=March 20, 2013 |title=''Arrow''{{'s}} Manu Bennett Upped to Series Regular for Season 2 (Exclusive) |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/arrow-manu-bennett-season-2-430044/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220102102723/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/arrow-manu-bennett-season-2-430044/ |archive-date=January 2, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |work=The Hollywood Reporter}}</ref>
* [[John Barrowman]] as [[Malcolm Merlyn (Arrowverse)|Malcolm Merlyn / Dark Archer]] (seasons 3–4; recurring: seasons 1–2; guest: seasons 5–8),<ref>{{cite web |author=Jesse Schedeen |date=January 6, 2016 |title=Arrow's John Barrowman to Write Dark Archer Comic |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2016/01/06/arrows-john-barrowman-to-write-dark-archer-comic |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160204052724/http://www.ign.com/articles/2016/01/06/arrows-john-barrowman-to-write-dark-archer-comic |archive-date=February 4, 2016 |access-date=January 28, 2016 |work=IGN}}</ref> a wealthy businessman, the father of Tommy and Thea, and Oliver's nemesis. He is based on the DC Comics character [[Merlyn (DC Comics)|Merlyn]]. After being a recurring guest star for the first two seasons, Barrowman became a series regular in season three.<ref>{{cite web |last=Ng |first=Philiana |date=May 15, 2014 |title=''Arrow'': John Barrowman Promoted to Series Regular for Season 3 |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/arrow-john-barrowman-series-regular-704413 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140517192014/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/arrow-john-barrowman-series-regular-704413 |archive-date=May 17, 2014 |access-date=May 15, 2014 |work=The Hollywood Reporter}}</ref> Barrowman reprised the role in season five during the crossover event "[[Invasion! (Arrowverse)|Invasion!]]" and later with his character's apparent death occurring off-screen, and again in season seven's crossover "[[Elseworlds (Arrowverse)|Elseworlds]]" as a hallucination.<ref>{{Cite web |date=November 11, 2018 |title=John Barrowman Confirms Return In Arrow Season 7 |url=https://www.cinemablend.com/television/2461181/john-barrowman-confirms-return-in-arrow-season-7 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190201065731/https://www.cinemablend.com/television/2461181/john-barrowman-confirms-return-in-arrow-season-7 |archive-date=February 1, 2019 |access-date=February 1, 2019 |website=CINEMABLEND}}</ref>
* [[Echo Kellum]] as [[Curtis Holt (Arrowverse)|Curtis Holt / Mister Terrific]] (seasons 5–7; recurring: season 4; guest: season 8), based on the DC Comics character of the [[Mister Terrific (Michael Holt)|same name]]. Holt is a technological savant, inventor and medal-winning Olympic decathlete, who works with Felicity at Palmer Technologies.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Abrams |first=Natalie |date=July 17, 2015 |title=Arrow casts Mr. Terrific for season 4 |url=https://www.ew.com/article/2015/07/16/arrow-echo-kellum-mr-terrific-season-4 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180703015106/http://www.ew.com/article/2015/07/16/arrow-echo-kellum-mr-terrific-season-4 |archive-date=July 3, 2018 |access-date=July 17, 2015 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> Kellum was upgraded to series regular in the fifth season.<ref>{{cite web |last=Mitovich |first=Matt |date=April 4, 2016 |title='Arrow' Season 5: Echo Kellum promoted to Series Regular as Curtis Holt |url=http://tvline.com/2016/04/04/arrow-season-5-echo-kellum-series-regular-curtis/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160405065334/http://tvline.com/2016/04/04/arrow-season-5-echo-kellum-series-regular-curtis/ |archive-date=April 5, 2016 |access-date=May 26, 2016 |work=TVLine}}</ref> Kellum exited the series during season seven,<ref>{{Cite magazine |title='Arrow' star on their shocking exit from the show: 'It's not the end of [SPOILER]' |url=https://ew.com/tv/2019/02/11/arrow-echo-kellum-terrific-exit/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190801232110/https://ew.com/tv/2019/02/11/arrow-echo-kellum-terrific-exit/ |archive-date=August 1, 2019 |access-date=February 12, 2019 |magazine=Entertainment Weekly}}</ref> but returned for the finale and later appears as a guest star in season eight.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mitovich |first=Matt Webb |date=May 8, 2019 |title=Arrow Season Finale Photos Tease 3 Returns — Watch a Sneak Peek of Emily Bett Rickards' Final Episode |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/arrow-season-7-finale-photos-laurel-canary-curtis-bronze-tiger-1057923/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190514022146/https://tvline.com/2019/05/07/arrow-season-7-finale-photos-laurel-canary-curtis-bronze-tiger/ |archive-date=May 14, 2019 |access-date=May 14, 2019 |website=TVLine}}</ref>
* [[Josh Segarra]] as [[Adrian Chase (Arrowverse)|Adrian Chase / Prometheus]] (season 5; guest: seasons 6 & 8), Star City's new district attorney, who is later revealed to be season five's antagonist and a serial killer bent on seeking revenge against Oliver. He is based on the DC Comics characters [[Adrian Chase]] and [[Prometheus (DC Comics)|Prometheus]].<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Abrams |first=Natalie |date=March 1, 2017 |title=Arrow unveils Prometheus' identity&nbsp;— what's next? |url=https://ew.com/tv/2017/03/01/arrow-prometheus-identity-chase-spoilers/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170302062525/http://ew.com/tv/2017/03/01/arrow-prometheus-identity-chase-spoilers/ |archive-date=March 2, 2017 |access-date=March 1, 2017 |magazine=Entertainment Weekly}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title='Arrow' Fans Are Loving SPOILER's Return in "Fundamentals" |url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/04/13/arrow-season-6-episode-18-adrian-chase-returns/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180521065811/http://comicbook.com/dc/2018/04/13/arrow-season-6-episode-18-adrian-chase-returns/ |archive-date=May 21, 2018 |access-date=May 20, 2018 |work=DC}}</ref>
* [[Rick Gonzalez]] as [[Rene Ramirez|Rene Ramirez / Wild Dog]] (seasons 6–8; recurring: season 5), a dishonorably discharged Marine with an estranged daughter who joins Oliver's vigilante team. He is based on the DC Comics character of the same name. Gonzalez was promoted to series regular from season six.<ref name="Deadline Hollywood">{{cite web |date=April 13, 2017 |title=Arrow Ups Rick Gonzalez & Juliana Harkavy To Season 6 Regulars |url=https://deadline.com/2017/04/arrow-rick-gonzalez-juliana-harkavy-wild-dog-black-canary-promoted-season-6-regulars-1202068856/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170518031146/http://deadline.com/2017/04/arrow-rick-gonzalez-juliana-harkavy-wild-dog-black-canary-promoted-season-6-regulars-1202068856/ |archive-date=May 18, 2017 |access-date=October 12, 2018 |work=Deadline Hollywood}}</ref>
* [[Juliana Harkavy]] as [[Dinah Drake (Arrowverse)|Dinah Drake / Black Canary]] (seasons 6–8; recurring: season 5), an undercover detective in Central City who later joins Oliver's team, taking on the Black Canary mantle. Harkavy was promoted to series regular from season six.<ref name="Deadline Hollywood"/>
* [[Kirk Acevedo]] as Ricardo Diaz (season 7; recurring: season 6), a drug lord recently released from incarceration who terrorizes Star City, and targets Oliver. Acevedo was promoted to series regular for season seven.<ref>{{cite web |last=Pedersen |first=Erik |date=October 11, 2018 |title='Arrow': Kirk Acevedo Upped To Series Regular For Season 7 On The CW |url=https://deadline.com/2018/10/arrow-kirk-acevedo-upped-to-series-regular-for-season-7-on-the-cw-1202481369/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181012033237/https://deadline.com/2018/10/arrow-kirk-acevedo-upped-to-series-regular-for-season-7-on-the-cw-1202481369/ |archive-date=October 12, 2018 |access-date=October 12, 2018 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref>
* [[Sea Shimooka]] as [[Emiko Queen (Arrowverse)|Emiko Queen / Green Arrow]] (season 7; guest: season 8), Oliver's paternal half-sister and a vigilante who takes over the Green Arrow mantle after Oliver's imprisonment.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Agard |first=Chancellor |date=December 3, 2018 |title=Arrow recap: The new Green Arrow is unmasked! |url=https://ew.com/recap/arrow-season-7-episode-8/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181204143258/https://ew.com/recap/arrow-season-7-episode-8/ |archive-date=December 4, 2018 |access-date=December 3, 2018 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref>
