''Arrow'' premiered on The CW network from October 10, 2012, during the [[2012–13 United States network television schedule|2012–13 television season]].<ref name="StartDateUK">{{cite web |title=Sky announces 2012 season premier this Autumn |url=http://sky1.sky.com/arrow/arrow-to-come-to-sky1-hd |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120930180631/http://sky1.sky.com/arrow/arrow-to-come-to-sky1-hd |archive-date=September 30, 2012 |access-date=September 29, 2012 |work=SkyOne}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Gorman |first=Bill |date=May 17, 2012 |title=CW 2012–13 Primetime Schedule: 'Supernatural' To Wednesday, 'Nikita' To 9pm, 'Beauty & the Beast' Follows 'Vampire Diaries' & Lots More Changes |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2012/05/17/cw-2011-12-primetime-schedule-supernatural-to-wednesday-nikita-to-9pm-beauty-the-beast-follows-vampire-diaries-lots-more-changes/134657 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120815193426/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2012/05/17/cw-2011-12-primetime-schedule-supernatural-to-wednesday-nikita-to-9pm-beauty-the-beast-follows-vampire-diaries-lots-more-changes/134657/ |archive-date=August 15, 2012 |access-date=August 18, 2012 |work=TV By the Numbers}}</ref> In Canada, the show is [[Simultaneous substitution|broadcast simultaneously]] on the same day as the United States.<ref>{{cite web |title=CTV |url=http://www.bellmediapr.ca/ctv/releases/release.asp?id=15184 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://archive.today/20120720181739/http://www.bellmediapr.ca/ctv/releases/release.asp?id=15184 |archive-date=July 20, 2012 |work=Bell Media}}</ref> The show premiered outside North America throughout the United Kingdom and Ireland,<ref>{{cite news |date=July 11, 2013 |title=Summer Glau joins the cast of 'Arrow' |url=http://www.rte.ie/ten/news/2013/0711/461879-summer-glau-joins-cast-of-arrow/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130928124211/http://www.rte.ie/ten/news/2013/0711/461879-summer-glau-joins-cast-of-arrow/ |archive-date=September 28, 2013 |access-date=August 28, 2013 |work=RTÉ News}}</ref> on October 22, 2012.<ref>{{cite web |last=Lambert |first=David |date=April 3, 2013 |title=Arrow&nbsp;– Blu-rays, DVDs for {{'}}''The Complete 1st Season''{{'}}: Date, Cost, Packaging, More! |url=http://www.tvshowsondvd.com/news/Arrow-Season-1/18147 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130528070113/http://www.tvshowsondvd.com/news/Arrow-Season-1/18147 |archive-date=May 28, 2013 |access-date=May 16, 2013 |work=TV Shows on DVD}}</ref> In Australia, the series premiered on May 1, 2013,<ref>{{cite web |date=April 20, 2013 |title=Airdate: Arrow. Bumped: The Following |url=http://www.tvtonight.com.au/2013/04/airdate-arrow-bumped-the-following.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130927223253/http://www.tvtonight.com.au/2013/04/airdate-arrow-bumped-the-following.html |archive-date=September 27, 2013 |access-date=October 6, 2013 |work=TV Tonight}}</ref> on the [[Nine Network]], before moving to [[Foxtel]] for Season 4.<ref>{{cite web |last=Turner |first=Adam |date=September 23, 2015 |title=Foxtel snaps up Marvel's Agents of SHIELD as more free-to-air TV locked away |url=https://www.smh.com.au/technology/foxtel-snaps-up-marvels-agents-of-shield-as-more-freetoair-tv-locked-away-20150923-gjt3dq.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220103000903/https://www.smh.com.au/technology/foxtel-snaps-up-marvels-agents-of-shield-as-more-freetoair-tv-locked-away-20150923-gjt3dq.html |archive-date=January 3, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |url-access=limited |work=The Sydney Morning Herald}}</ref>

===Home media===
{{See also|List of Arrow episodes#Home media}}
Each season release contains additional features, which include: making-of featurettes, episode commentaries, deleted scenes, gag reels, Comic-Con panels, and highlights from the Paley Fest. Starting with season four and continuing through each subsequent season, the boxsets included the crossover episodes from other connected series, as well as commentary on those episodes.

