In the United States, ''Arrow''{{'}}s premiere episode drew 4.14 million viewers, making it The CW's most-watched telecast of any show on any night in three years, and The CW's most-watched series premiere since ''[[The Vampire Diaries]]'' in 2009. In its second episode, ''Arrow'' became the only new network drama in the 2012–13 season to hold its ratings in both adults 18–34 and adults 18–49 from its premiere to its second week.<ref name="S1Pickup"/> In Australia, the premiere received 1.32 million viewers, making it the third most-watched broadcast on the network that night.<ref>{{cite web |last=Knox |first=David |date=May 2, 2013 |title=Wednesday 1 May 2013 |url=http://www.tvtonight.com.au/2013/05/wednesday-1-may-2013.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150325205719/http://www.tvtonight.com.au/2013/05/wednesday-1-may-2013.html |archive-date=March 25, 2015 |access-date=February 20, 2015 |work=TV Tonight}}</ref> The UK broadcast was the highest-rated telecast of the week on [[Sky 1]], with 1.85 million viewers.<ref>{{cite web |title=Weekly Top 30 |url=https://www.barb.co.uk/whats-new/weekly-top-30 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101215200025/http://www.barb.co.uk/report/weeklyTopProgrammesOverview |archive-date=December 15, 2010 |access-date=February 20, 2015 |work=BARB}} Note: The ratings must be searched for.</ref> In Canada, the first episode got 1.32 million viewers, making it the fourth most-watched airing of the night and the twenty-third of the week.<ref>{{cite web |date=October 15, 2012 |title=Top 30 Programs (October 8–14, 2012) |url=http://assets.numeris.ca/Downloads/October%208-15,%202012%20(Week%207).pdf |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150220212426/http://assets.numeris.ca/Downloads/October%208-15,%202012%20(Week%207).pdf |archive-date=February 20, 2015 |access-date=February 20, 2015 |work=Numeris}}</ref>

